  "description": "Issue #18 sprint 6 runtime-blocker-fix contract evidence (multi-locale build variant of locale-blank-sram-no-selector-default-modern-debug, SUPERSEDES the pre-fix locale-blank-sram-no-selector-multi-modern-debug scenario, which encoded the sprint-6 bug itself as 'expected' and has been deleted): booting the EXPANSION_ENABLED_LOCALES=en,qps-ploc EXPANSION_PSEUDO_LOCALE=1 modern debug ROM from a genuinely blank (all-0xFF) SRAM chip now correctly SHOWS the blocking first-start selector (active=1, promptShown=1, promptReason=1/UNSET, prefsState=0/UNSET, needsPreferenceRepair=1, enabledLocaleCount=2) and keeps it shown at frame 1400 with no player input given. Before this sprint's fix, BuildCurrentExpansionSaveMeta() (src/bmsave-lib.c) unconditionally stamped a syntactically VALID ExpansionUserPrefs record on every SAVE_COMPAT_EMPTY (blank-SRAM) boot regardless of FE8_EXPANSION_ENABLED_LOCALE_COUNT, so a genuinely fresh multi-locale save silently skipped the mandatory first-start locale prompt exactly like a single-locale build's AUTO_SELECT collapse -- this scenario is the real-capture proof that a multi-locale fresh save now blocks with the selector instead, matching locale-selector-multi-switch-qps-modern-debug's own real ExpansionUserPrefs UNSET fixture (which was never affected by this bug, since it forces the prefs record's raw bytes directly rather than going through the blank-SRAM stamp path -- see reports/issue18_localization_closure.md).",
